>> title: Espresso Brownies
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: chocolate, coffee, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: coffee brownies, mocha brownies
>> servings: 9
>> time: 50 min
>> source: Cooking for Engineers
>> step.7: bake 350°F (170°C) 30 to 40 min

Butter and flour an #8x8-in pan{}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (170°C).

Melt @unsalted butter{4%oz}(115 g).

Mix @&(~1)melted butter{} with @sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @vanilla extract{1/4%tsp}(2.5 mL), and @fresh brewed espresso{4%Tbs}(60 mL; or very strong coffee).

Mix @&(~1)mixture{} with @eggs{2%large}(100 g).

Fold in @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(80 g), @Hershey's cocoa powder{1/3%cup}(80 g), @baking soda{1/4%tsp}(1.3 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g) to @&(~1)batter{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} at 350°F for ~{30%min}.
